## Feature Name

Native CSS `text-decoration` Properties Animated Underline Collection

---

## Description

A focused collection of link and text underline animations built entirely on native CSS `text-decoration` sub-properties — `text-decoration-thickness`, `text-underline-offset`, `text-decoration-color`, and `text-decoration-style` — with CSS `transition`. No `::after` pseudo-element tricks, no `width: 0 → 100%` hacks.

Five variants are included:
1. **Lift** — underline rises away from the text baseline as it thickens
2. **Thick reveal** — underline fades in at full color while growing in thickness
3. **Color shift** — underline color transitions through a palette on hover
4. **Wavy appear** — underline style switches to `wavy` and color fades in
5. **Double line** — a `double` underline style reveals with offset animation

A side-by-side comparison section will show the `::after` pseudo-element approach breaking on wrapped multiline text, versus the native approach handling it correctly.

---

## Why is this useful for EaseMotion CSS?

The pseudo-element underline trick (`::after { width: 0 → 100% }`) is one of the most common patterns in CSS animation demos, including the existing `ease-hover-underline-grow` submission. However, it fundamentally breaks on multiline wrapped text — the underline only spans the last line. Native `text-decoration` sub-properties are animatable since mid-2022 across all major browsers and handle multiline text correctly by design. This collection demonstrates the spec-correct approach.

