## Feature Name

`mix-blend-mode: difference` Animated Inversion Sweep

---

## Description

A sweeping element with `mix-blend-mode: difference` passes across a card or section, inverting all colors directly beneath it as it travels. The result is a polished "scan line" or "light sweep" hover effect that inverts content colors dynamically — without touching a single color value in CSS. Three variants are included: a hover-triggered sweep, an infinite auto-sweep for loading/highlight states, and a `mix-blend-mode: exclusion` variant for a softer inversion.

The critical implementation detail — `isolation: isolate` on the parent container — will be demonstrated explicitly, with a side-by-side showing the bleed-to-background bug that occurs without it.

---

## Why is this useful for EaseMotion CSS?

`mix-blend-mode: difference` is one of the most visually striking single-property CSS techniques, used by Linear, Figma, and Apple for polished interactive effects. The existing blend-mode submissions in this repository cover static `multiply` overlays with hover opacity changes. An animated inversion sweep is a qualitatively different effect and a natural addition to the animation library.

