## Feature Name

CSS `@layer` Cascade Animation Priority — Interactive Visual Demo

---

## Description

A teaching demo that visualises how `@layer` ordering affects which `animation` declaration wins a cascade conflict on the same element. Three layers (`base`, `theme`, `override`) each define a different `animation` for the same `.demo-box` class. Visitors can see in real time how the layer order determines which keyframe plays — and discover that an **unlayered rule always beats any layered rule**, regardless of source order.

Pure CSS checkboxes (using `:checked` + adjacent sibling selectors) toggle each layer's effect on/off without JavaScript.

---

## Why is this useful for EaseMotion CSS?

EaseMotion CSS is built on `@layer` (the repo's enhancement issue calls for wrapping components in `@layer easemotion-components`). Understanding layer cascade priority is therefore fundamental to contributors. This demo makes an abstract spec rule viscerally obvious through motion — when the layer order changes, a different animation plays on the exact same element.

---

## HTML Snippet

