## Feature Name

CSS-Only Animated Bar / Column Chart — Pure CSS Data Visualisation

---

## Description

A fully CSS-only bar chart where bars grow from zero to their final height on page load, using `transform: scaleY()` + `transform-origin: bottom center` + `animation-delay: calc(var(--i) * 80ms)` for a staggered entrance. Each bar's height is encoded as a CSS custom property on the element's inline `style` attribute, making it trivial to set values from static HTML with no JavaScript.

A horizontal bar variant uses the same pattern with `scaleX()` and `transform-origin: left center`. Tooltips appear on `:hover` using adjacent sibling CSS — zero JavaScript.

---

## Why is this useful for EaseMotion CSS?

Data visualisation in CSS is a genuinely underexplored area of animation. Many developers reach for charting libraries (Chart.js, D3) for simple bar stats that could be fully handled in CSS. This submission demonstrates that `transform-origin` + custom properties compose into a viable data chart primitive — and educates contributors on the `calc(var(--i) * delay)` stagger pattern.

