## Feature Name

CSS Tilt-Shift / Depth-of-Field Hero Section

---

## Description

A section layout that simulates tilt-shift photography — the technique where a camera's tilted lens plane creates a narrow band of sharp focus with progressive blur above and below it. Pure CSS achieves this with `filter: blur()` + `mask-image: linear-gradient()` on layered depth planes. A CSS custom property `--focus-y` controls where the in-focus band sits, and an auto-play animation pans it up and down, creating a "scanning camera" effect.

---

## Why is this useful for EaseMotion CSS?

Depth of field is one of the most evocative visual effects in photography and film. A CSS-only implementation gives designers a way to create this effect in hero sections, feature showcases, or photo galleries without WebGL, canvas, or image editing. It demonstrates `mask-image` compositing with `filter` — a powerful but underused combination.

---

## HTML Snippet

```html
<section class="tilt-shift-scene">
  <div class="depth-layer depth-layer--far">
    <p>Background content — buildings, landscape</p>
  </div>
  <div class="depth-layer depth-layer--mid">
    <p>Midground content — in focus band</p>
  </div>
  <div class="depth-layer depth-layer--near">
    <p>Foreground content — slightly blurred</p>
  </div>
</section>
```

---

## CSS Snippet

```css
@property --focus-y {
  syntax: '<percentage>';
  initial-value: 50%;
  inherits: true;
}

.tilt-shift-scene {
  position: relative;
  width: 100%;
  height: 400px;
  overflow: hidden;
  border-radius: 16px;
  --focus-y: 50%;
  animation: scan-focus 4s ease-in-out infinite alternate;
}

@keyframes scan-focus {
  from { --focus-y: 25%; }
  to   { --focus-y: 75%; }
}

.depth-layer {
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
}

/* Far layer: blurred, fading mask toward center */
.depth-layer--far {
  background: linear-gradient(to bottom, #1e3a5f 0%, #2d6a9f 100%);
  filter: blur(5px);
  mask-image: linear-gradient(
    to bottom,
    black 0%,
    black calc(var(--focus-y) - 20%),
    transparent calc(var(--focus-y) + 5%)
  );
  transform: scale(1.05); /* compensate blur edge bleed */
}

/* Mid layer: always sharp */
.depth-layer--mid {
  background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.06);
  backdrop-filter: blur(0px);
}

/* Near layer: blurred, fading mask from center downward */
.depth-layer--near {
  background: linear-gradient(to bottom, transparent, rgba(0, 80, 160, 0.5));
  filter: blur(3px);
  mask-image: linear-gradient(
    to bottom,
    transparent calc(var(--focus-y) - 5%),
    black calc(var(--focus-y) + 20%),
    black 100%
  );
}

@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  .tilt-shift-scene {
    animation: none;
    --focus-y: 50%;
  }
}
```

