## Description

`animation-composition` (Chrome 112+) controls how multiple animations compose on the same property — `replace` (default), `add`, or `accumulate`. This is completely absent from the repo. The practical problem it solves: a card that has a continuous floating `@keyframes` animation on `transform` loses that animation the moment a hover animation takes over the same property (because default `replace` overwrites it). With `animation-composition: accumulate` on the hover animation, both stack — the float continues while the hover lift adds on top.

