---

## Description

CSS 2023 shipped `linear()` — a timing function that accepts N value stops to approximate any arbitrary curve, including under-damped spring physics with overshoot. Unlike `cubic-bezier()` which maxes out at 4 control points, `linear(0, 0.009, 0.035 6.1%, 0.141, 0.281 18.4%, 0.723 30.7%, 0.875, 0.969, 1.02, 1.048 44.1%, 1.063, 1.047, 1.018 59.6%, 1.008, 0.999, 0.998 72.5%, 1)` encodes a full spring response. This submission showcases three spring presets (snappy, wobbly, stiff) applied to practical UI animations, with a side-by-side comparison against `ease-out`.

