## Why is this useful for EaseMotion CSS?

The existing spring utility uses cubic-bezier approximations. `linear()` is the actual solution — it encodes the spring curve directly, no approximation. It's also composable: store the value in a custom property and swap it across any animation. This is a gap in the current easing coverage.

