A card component with an animated folded corner (dog-ear) using only CSS pseudo-elements. The fold is constructed with a CSS border triangle on `::after` and a "paper underside" on `::before`. On hover, the fold grows larger using a `transition` on `border-width`. The animation runs on entrance as well.

No JS, no extra DOM elements beyond the card itself.

---

## Why is this useful for EaseMotion CSS?

It is a practical, immediately recognizable UI pattern — sticky note cards, pricing cards marked as "recommended", document previews. The CSS border-triangle technique for making the fold is non-obvious (most developers reach for SVG or absolute-positioned triangles instead). A working reference submission would be genuinely useful.

