## Feature Name

Mosaic Tile Scatter Entrance

---

## Description

A CSS grid where each cell flies in from a different cardinal direction and lands in its position, creating the impression of tiles assembling a mosaic. The origin direction rotates per `nth-child` using CSS custom properties — so tile 1 comes from the left, tile 2 from the top, tile 3 from the right, tile 4 from the bottom, then it repeats. Combined with a per-tile `animation-delay`, the overall effect is of a mosaic self-assembling.

This is different from the stagger submissions already in the repo, which all use a single direction (typically fade-up). The distinguishing feature here is the four-directional origin pattern derived purely from `nth-child` modulo arithmetic.

---

## Why is this useful for EaseMotion CSS?

Portfolio grids, image galleries, feature card sections — anywhere a grid reveals content. The multi-directional approach is visually more dynamic than a uniform fade-up stagger and requires the same amount of markup.

---

## HTML Snippet

```html
