## Feature Name

SVG Text Stroke Draw-On Animation

---

## Description

Animate `stroke-dashoffset` on an SVG `<text>` element to produce a "draw-on" handwriting/outline effect. The text starts as an invisible outlined stroke and the stroke is progressively revealed using a `stroke-dasharray` / `stroke-dashoffset` keyframe. After the stroke is fully drawn, `fill-opacity` animates from 0 to 1 to flood-fill the letters.

The existing `ease-svg-path-draw-v1` submission does this for shape paths (icons, vectors). Applying it to `<text>` with `fill: none` and a visible `stroke` is a different use case with no existing coverage.

---

## Why is this useful for EaseMotion CSS?

This is one of the most requested CSS effects for hero sections and loading screens. An outlined headline that draws itself in is memorable and works especially well on dark backgrounds. Pure CSS handles the animation — no JS or SMIL.

---

## HTML Snippet

```html
<!-- Basic draw-on -->
<svg class="ease-text-draw-svg" viewBox="0 0 800 120" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
  <text class="ease-text-draw" x="50%" y="80" text-anchor="middle">EASEⓂ</text>
</svg>

<!-- Draw then fill -->
<svg class="ease-text-draw-svg" viewBox="0 0 800 120" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
  <text class="ease-text-draw ease-text-draw--fill" x="50%" y="80" text-anchor="middle">MOTION</text>
</svg>

<!-- Looping erase-and-redraw -->
<svg class="ease-text-draw-svg" viewBox="0 0 800 120" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
  <text class="ease-text-draw ease-text-draw--loop" x="50%" y="80" text-anchor="middle">CSS</text>
</svg>
```

---

## CSS Snippet

```css
.ease-text-draw-svg {
  width: 100%;
  max-width: 800px;
  overflow: visible;
}

.ease-text-draw {
  fill: none;
  stroke: #ffffff;
  stroke-width: 1.5px;
  font-size: 80px;
  font-weight: 900;
  font-family: system-ui, sans-serif;
  letter-spacing: 0.05em;

  stroke-dasharray: 2000;
  stroke-dashoffset: 2000;
  animation: text-draw 2.4s ease-out both;
}

@keyframes text-draw {
  to { stroke-dashoffset: 0; }
}

/* Fill variant — flood-fills after stroke completes */
.ease-text-draw--fill {
  animation: text-draw 2.4s ease-out forwards, text-fill 0.6s ease-in 2.4s forwards;
  fill: #ffffff;
  fill-opacity: 0;
}

@keyframes text-fill {
  to { fill-opacity: 1; }
}

/* Glow variant */
.ease-text-draw--glow {
  stroke: #818cf8;
  filter: drop-shadow(0 0 6px #818cf8) drop-shadow(0 0 14px #6366f1);
}

/* Loop variant */
.ease-text-draw--loop {
  animation: text-draw-loop 4s ease-in-out infinite;
}

@keyframes text-draw-loop {
  0%   { stroke-dashoffset: 2000; }
  45%  { stroke-dashoffset: 0; }
  55%  { stroke-dashoffset: 0; }
  100% { stroke-dashoffset: 2000; }
}

@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  .ease-text-draw { animation: none; stroke-dashoffset: 0; }
  .ease-text-draw--fill { fill-opacity: 1; }
}
```

