## Feature Name

Chromatic Aberration RGB Text Split

---

## Description

A CSS-only RGB channel-split effect on text using `::before`/`::after` pseudo-elements with `color: red` / `color: blue` and `mix-blend-mode: screen`. The pseudo-elements mirror the text via `content: attr(data-text)` and are offset horizontally. Animating the offset creates the impression that the red, green, and blue channels of the text are misaligned — like a lens or old VHS tape.

This is mechanistically different from the glitch submissions in this repo. Those use `clip-path` displacement on block elements. This works at the color channel level on text specifically.

---

## Why is this useful for EaseMotion CSS?

It is a high-impact visual effect with a clear, targeted use case: dark-mode hero text, error states, cyberpunk/tech aesthetic UIs. The technique requires zero JS, zero SVG, and fits perfectly into the single-class philosophy.

---

## HTML Snippet

```html
<!-- data-text must match the element's text content -->
<h1 class="ease-chroma" data-text="ABERRANT">ABERRANT</h1>

<h2 class="ease-chroma ease-chroma--subtle" data-text="EaseMotion">EaseMotion</h2>

<h2 class="ease-chroma ease-chroma--hover" data-text="Hover Me">Hover Me</h2>
```

---

## CSS Snippet

```css
/* Requires a dark background to work correctly with mix-blend-mode: screen */
.ease-chroma {
  position: relative;
  color: #ffffff;
  font-weight: 900;
}

.ease-chroma::before,
.ease-chroma::after {
  content: attr(data-text);
  position: absolute;
  top: 0;
  left: 0;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  mix-blend-mode: screen;
  animation-timing-function: ease-in-out;
  animation-iteration-count: infinite;
}

.ease-chroma::before {
  color: #ff0000;
  animation: chroma-r 2.5s infinite;
}

.ease-chroma::after {
  color: #0000ff;
  animation: chroma-b 2.5s infinite;
}

@keyframes chroma-r {
  0%, 100% { transform: translate(-3px, 0); }
  33%       { transform: translate(2px, 1px); }
  66%       { transform: translate(-1px, -1px); }
}

@keyframes chroma-b {
  0%, 100% { transform: translate(3px, 0); }
  33%       { transform: translate(-2px, -1px); }
  66%       { transform: translate(1px, 1px); }
}

/* Subtle variant — smaller offsets */
.ease-chroma--subtle::before { animation-name: chroma-r-subtle; }
.ease-chroma--subtle::after  { animation-name: chroma-b-subtle; }

@keyframes chroma-r-subtle {
  0%, 100% { transform: translate(-1px, 0); }
  50%       { transform: translate(1px, 0); }
}
@keyframes chroma-b-subtle {
  0%, 100% { transform: translate(1px, 0); }
  50%       { transform: translate(-1px, 0); }
}

/* Hover-only variant */
.ease-chroma--hover::before,
.ease-chroma--hover::after { animation: none; }
.ease-chroma--hover:hover::before { animation: chroma-r 0.6s infinite; }
.ease-chroma--hover:hover::after  { animation: chroma-b 0.6s infinite; }

@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  .ease-chroma::before,
  .ease-chroma::after { animation: none; }
}
```

