## Description

A row of tall rectangular elements that fall forward sequentially, each rotating 90deg around its bottom edge (`transform-origin: center bottom`) with a staggered `animation-delay`. The trigger is a hover on the parent container or a CSS checkbox. The result looks like a real domino chain reaction. Nothing like this exists in the current submissions — stagger animations here all use fade/translate, not a physical toppling rotation from a base axis.

