2. Navigate to `/contact`.
3. Scroll down to the map section.
4. Observe the shimmer skeleton spinning indefinitely — the map never appears and no error state is shown.

### Expected Behavior

After a reasonable timeout, or on load failure, the loading state should resolve and display a static fallback such as the address text with a "View on Google Maps" link.

### Suggested Fix

Add an `onError` handler and a timeout fallback:

```jsx
function MapSection() {
  const [loaded, setLoaded] = useState(false);
  const [failed, setFailed] = useState(false);
  const timeoutRef = useRef(null);

  useEffect(() => {
    if (show) {
      timeoutRef.current = setTimeout(() => {
        setFailed(true);
        setLoaded(true);
      }, 10000);
    }
    return () => clearTimeout(timeoutRef.current);
  }, [show]);

  const handleLoad = () => {
    clearTimeout(timeoutRef.current);
    setLoaded(true);
  };

  const handleError = () => {
    clearTimeout(timeoutRef.current);
    setFailed(true);
    setLoaded(true);
  };

