2. Navigate to any event detail page.
3. Immediately press the browser back button or navigate to another route.
4. Observe the React warning about a state update on an unmounted component in the console (visible in development/strict mode).

### Expected Behavior

The `setTimeout` should be cancelled when the component unmounts so no state update fires after teardown.

### Suggested Fix

```js
useEffect(() => {
  window.scrollTo({ top: 0 });
  const tid = setTimeout(() => setMounted(true), 60);

  const obs = new IntersectionObserver(...);
  document.querySelectorAll('...').forEach((el) => obs.observe(el));

  return () => {
    clearTimeout(tid);
    obs.disconnect();
  };
}, []);
```

