## Why is this useful for EaseMotion CSS?

Existing tilt card submissions (e.g. `parallax-tilt-effect-v1`, `3d-tilt-card`) rely on JavaScript `mousemove` event listeners to calculate real-time tilt based on cursor position. A pure-CSS version using fixed `rotate3d` values on `:hover` is simpler, lighter, and immediately composable with any EaseMotion class — no script tag required. It fills a distinct gap as the no-JS alternative.

