- `server/src/modules/roadmap/controller.js` — `syncRoadmap` (line 36), `addTutorMilestone` (line ~440), `assignTutorResource` (line ~230)

**Suggested fix:**

```js
// 1. Schema level — server/src/database/models/LearningProgress.js
topicName: {
  type: String,
  required: true,
  maxlength: [200, "Topic name must not exceed 200 characters"],
  trim: true,
},

// 2. Controller level — syncRoadmap validation block
for (const topic of topics) {
  const name = typeof topic === "string" ? topic : (topic.text || topic.topicName || "");
  if (name.length > 200) {
    throw new AppError("Each topic name must not exceed 200 characters", 400);
  }
}

// 3. addTutorMilestone — add after existing duplicate check
if (topicName.trim().length > 200) {
  throw new AppError("Topic name must not exceed 200 characters", 400);
}
```

Applying the constraint at both layers (schema + controller) follows the defense-in-depth pattern already used elsewhere in this codebase (e.g., `coverLetterValidation.js` which sets `maxLength: 5000` on `jobDescription`).

## Description

In `src/hooks/useSessions.ts`, XP for `session_join` is awarded in **two separate, independent places** with no cross-guard between them:

1. **`handleJoinSession`** (line ~201) — awarded when a user clicks the "Join Session" button, guarded by an `existingParticipant` check:
```ts
if (!existingParticipant) {
  awardXP({ activity: "session_join" });
}
```

2. **`handleJoinVideo`** (lines ~288–292) — awarded when a user clicks "Join Video", with **no guard at all**:
```ts
const handleJoinVideo = useCallback(() => {
  setIsVideoActive(true);
  awardXP({ activity: 'session_join' }); // fires unconditionally every time
}, [awardXP]);
```

A user can exploit this in two ways:
- **Double award**: Join a session (50 XP) then click "Join Video" (another 50 XP) → **100 XP total** for a single session
- **Infinite farming**: Click "Leave Video" → click "Join Video" again → earn 50 XP each time with no limit

The comment in the code even acknowledges the missing guard:
```ts
// Simple mock logic for preventing double XP without using localStorage here directly unless needed
```

## Steps to Reproduce

1. Log in and navigate to the Sessions page.
2. Join any available session → observe 50 XP awarded.
3. In the session view, click the **"Join Video"** button → observe another 50 XP awarded.
4. Click **"Leave"** on the video room to exit.
5. Click **"Join Video"** again → observe another 50 XP.
6. Repeat steps 4–5 to farm unlimited XP.

## Expected Behavior

`session_join` XP should be awarded **at most once per session per user**. `handleJoinVideo` should not award any additional XP, as the join event is already covered by `handleJoinSession`.

## Actual Behavior

Clicking "Join Video" awards 50 XP on every invocation regardless of whether `session_join` XP was already awarded for that session. There is no cooldown, deduplication, or per-session guard.

## Root Cause

`handleJoinVideo` in `src/hooks/useSessions.ts` calls `awardXP({ activity: 'session_join' })` unconditionally. Unlike `handleJoinSession`, which checks the database for an existing participant record before awarding XP, `handleJoinVideo` has no equivalent guard.

## Suggested Fix

Track which session IDs have already received video-join XP using a `useRef<Set<string>>`, and only award XP on the first video join per session:

```ts
const videoXPAwardedRef = useRef<Set<string>>(new Set());

const handleJoinVideo = useCallback(() => {
  setIsVideoActive(true);
  if (selectedSession && !videoXPAwardedRef.current.has(selectedSession.id)) {
    videoXPAwardedRef.current.add(selectedSession.id);
    awardXP({ activity: 'session_join' });
  }
}, [awardXP, selectedSession]);
```

Alternatively, remove the XP award from `handleJoinVideo` entirely, since `handleJoinSession` already handles it.

## Impact

- Leaderboard rankings are distorted for users who exploit this to farm XP.
- Badges and achievements gated on XP thresholds can be reached without genuine participation.
- The gamification system loses its integrity across the platform.

## Description

