## Description

A submission under `submissions/examples/segmented-control/` that implements a segmented control (a row of mutually exclusive toggle buttons) using only CSS — no JavaScript. Uses the checkbox/radio hack: hidden `<input type="radio">` elements paired with `<label>` elements, with the selected segment styled via `:checked + label` or the `<label for>` association. Common use cases include view switchers (List / Grid / Map), time-range pickers (Day / Week / Month), and filter tabs.

---

## Why is this useful for EaseMotion CSS?

Segmented controls are a staple mobile and desktop UI pattern that almost every app needs. Pure CSS implementations are rare and often undiscovered — having a canonical submission example here makes it easy for contributors and end-users to copy-paste a working, accessible, zero-JS control without reaching for a JavaScript framework component.

