## 🐞 Description

Product cards render star ratings using a `for (let i = 0; i < p.rating; i++)` loop with float values. Because JavaScript's `<` operator compares against the raw decimal, a rating of `4.2` causes the loop to execute **5 times** (since `4 < 4.2 === true`), displaying a full 5-star rating instead of the correct ~4 stars. This inflates every fractional rating above an integer boundary.

All products with ids 17–32 in `products.js` have fractional ratings (4.0 to 4.7) and are affected.

---

## 🔁 Steps to Reproduce

1. Open `shop.html` or `index.html`
2. Find any product with a fractional rating such as "Indigo Denim Jacket" (id: 20, rating: 4.7) or "Olive Cargo Utility Pants" (id: 18, rating: 4.2)
3. Observe the star rating displayed on the product card
4. See that 5 full stars are shown instead of the correct 4 stars

---

## 💻 Expected Behavior

A product with a rating of `4.2` should display **4 full stars** (and optionally a half-star). A rating of `4.7` should display **4 full stars + 1 half-star**. Only a rating of exactly `5.0` should show 5 full stars.

---

## 🧠 Actual Behavior

Any product with a rating between `4.0` (exclusive) and `5.0` (inclusive) displays **5 full stars** due to the loop condition `i < p.rating` being `true` on the 5th iteration when rating is e.g. `4.2`.

---

## 🖼️ Screenshots / Logs (if applicable)

**Affected file:** `products.js`, lines 87–93

```js
// Current buggy code
const starDiv = document.createElement('div');
starDiv.className = 'star';
for (let i = 0; i < p.rating; i++) {   // ← float comparison causes extra iteration
  const starIcon = document.createElement('i');
  starIcon.className = 'ri-star-fill';
  starDiv.appendChild(starIcon);
}
```

**Suggested fix:**
```js
const fullStars = Math.floor(p.rating);
const hasHalf  = (p.rating % 1) >= 0.5;
for (let i = 0; i < fullStars; i++) {
  const star = document.createElement('i');
  star.className = 'ri-star-fill';
  starDiv.appendChild(star);
}
if (hasHalf) {
  const half = document.createElement('i');
  half.className = 'ri-star-half-fill';
  starDiv.appendChild(half);
}
```

