The `collab:ai_continue` socket event handler emits a hardcoded placeholder string instead of calling the actual Gemini AI service. The AI continuation feature in collaborative rooms is non-functional:

```ts
socket.on("collab:ai_continue", ({ roomId }) => {
  const room = rooms.get(roomId);
  if (!room) return;

  collabNamespace.to(roomId).emit("collab:ai_thinking", { roomId });

  const aiChunk: IStoryChunk = {
    authorId: "ai",
    authorName: "✨ AI",
    color: "#d4af37",
    text: "...the story continues with AI magic here...",  // ← hardcoded stub
    isAI: true,
    timestamp: new Date(),
  };

  room.story.push(aiChunk);
  collabNamespace.to(roomId).emit("collab:story_updated", { story: room.story, newChunk: aiChunk });
});
```

When a user clicks "AI Continue" in a collab room, the literal string `"...the story continues with AI magic here..."` is appended to the collaborative story. The actual `AiModelService` (which calls Gemini) is never invoked.

> **Note:** This is distinct from issue #726 ("Add AI Story Continuation Engine for Multi-Chapter AI Stories"), which is a new feature request for chapter-based story continuation in the single-user flow. This issue is about the existing collab room handler that is already wired up in the UI but returns a stub instead of real AI output.

**Impact:** The AI-assisted collaborative writing feature — one of the core value propositions of the collab mode — is completely broken. Users get a placeholder string in their story.

### Steps to reproduce

1. Start the backend server
2. Open the Collab page in the frontend
3. Create or join a collab room
4. Click the "AI Continue" button
5. Observe that the text `"...the story continues with AI magic here..."` is appended to the story instead of an AI-generated continuation

### Proposed fix

Replace the stub with a real call to `AiModelService.aiFreeModelGenerate` (or the authenticated variant), using the current room story as context for the prompt:

```ts
socket.on("collab:ai_continue", async ({ roomId }) => {
  const room = rooms.get(roomId);
  if (!room) return;

  collabNamespace.to(roomId).emit("collab:ai_thinking", { roomId });

  try {
    // Build a continuation prompt from the existing story
    const storyContext = room.story.map(c => c.text).join(" ");
    const prompt = {
      prompt: `Continue this collaborative story naturally in 2-3 sentences: ${storyContext}`,
      language: "English",
    };

    const result = await AiModelService.aiFreeModelGenerate(prompt);
    const continuationText = result?.[0]?.story ?? "The story continues...";

    const aiChunk: IStoryChunk = {
      authorId: "ai",
      authorName: "✨ AI",
      color: "#d4af37",
      text: continuationText,
      isAI: true,
      timestamp: new Date(),
    };

    room.story.push(aiChunk);
    collabNamespace.to(roomId).emit("collab:story_updated", { story: room.story, newChunk: aiChunk });
  } catch {
    collabNamespace.to(roomId).emit("collab:error", { message: "AI continuation failed. Please try again." });
  }
});
```

